+ what is linux
- It is the core kernel of an operating system. Complete systems bundle the kernel with utilities and user interfaces, known as distributions (distros).

+ is linux free
- Yes. The source code is free to use, study, and change under the GNU General Public License.

+ what is a distribution
- Popular versions like Linux Mint, Ubuntu, or Fedora package the Linux kernel with apps and desktop tools.

+ will linux run on my pc
- Linux runs on almost all standard PC hardware, Intel, AMD, and ARM processors.

+ how do i use the terminal
- Open the command-line interface to type text commands directly to the shell.
- Type text commands here to run them in the shell.

+ commands
- Tab-completion can help you complete command names in the shell - by pressing tab.

+ what are the command names
@ commands

+ what are all [of] the commands
@ commands

+ manual [page]
- Try typing "man man" for the manual for the manual program - man.

+ how do i (use|run) *
@ manual

+ how do i (use|run) the (command|program) *
@ manual

+ what are the [basic] commands
- Use "ls" to list files, "cd" to change folders, and "pwd" to see your current folder path.

+ how do i exit *
- Sometimes a program can be cancelled by pressing ctrl+c, sometimes by pressing the escape key, or by typing :q.

